ts should (i) an earned and recognised Master's degree in relevant disciplines; (ii) relevant teaching / professional experience; and a good command of English and Chinese is required. Preference will be given to those with teaching experience in degree programmes / proven research record. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required as appropriate for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Professor (Film and Creative Entertainment), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref: 26/119/DES/ACAD) Duties Lead and participate in the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in Film and Creative Entertainment Programme.. Conduct research in the relevant discipline and related areas that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; Engage in industrial and community partnership engagement and other scholarly and professional activities; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School, the Provost and the President Appointment Criteria A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in their field, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in their respective areas. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Professor (Design), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref: 26/118/DES/ACAD) Duties Lead and participate in the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in Design Programme. Conduct research in the relevant discipline and related areas that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; Engage in industrial and community partnership engagement and other scholarly and professional activities; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School, the Provost and the President Appointment Criteria A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in their field, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in their field and related areas; Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in their respective areas. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Professor (Ref: 26/116/ACAD) Duties Lead and participate in the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in the relevant discipline and related areas at postgraduate, undergraduate and sub-degree levels; Conduct research in the relevant discipline and related areas that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; Engage in industrial and community partnership engagement and other scholarly and professional activities; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School, the Provost and the President. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have: A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in their field, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in their field and related areas; Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in their respective areas. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Senior Lecturers/ Lecturers, Faith Hope Love Department of General Education (Ref: 26/111/GELS/ACAD) Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching General Education courses at degree/sub-degree (Higher Diploma / Associate Degree) / diploma levels in the following areas: Philosophy Humanities Cultural Studies General Education Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) Master's degree holders will be considered for the post at Lecturer grade); and (ii) relevant teaching/ professional experience. Preference will be given to those with experience in curriculum design, programme development and management. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required as appropriate for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Professor in Physiotherapy, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences  (Ref: 26/105/HS/ACAD/ICEC) Duties The appointee will be required to: Provide leadership and steer the development and operation of the Integrated Clinical Education Centre (ICEC) and contribute to the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in the relevant discipline at postgraduate, undergraduate, and sub-degree levels; Contribute to the advancement of physiotherapy education and related disciplines through innovative teaching and curriculum development; Undertake teaching activities at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; Initiate, lead, and conduct research and consultancy that result in publications in top-tier refereed journals and other scholarly outputs; Engage in industrial and community partnership activities and other professional collaborations; Undertake relevant academic and administrative duties and contribute to the effective operation of the School; and Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School of Health Sciences, the Provost, the President, or their delegates. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have: A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in their field, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in their field and related areas; Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in their respective areas. Applicants for appointment at Professor level should have substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience in physiotherapy and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment as Associate or Assistant Professor. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Professor, Yam Pak Charitable Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref: 26/98/CIS/ACAD) Duties Lead and participate in the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in Computing and Information Sciences and related areas at postgraduate, undergraduate and sub-degree levels; Conduct research in Computing and Information Sciences and related areas that leads to publications in top-tier referred journals; Engage in industrial partnership engagement and other scholarly and professional activities; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School, the Provost and the President. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have: A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in Computing and Information Sciences, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in Computing and Information Sciences and related areas; Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in respective areas. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Professor/ Professor of Practice/ Associate Professor/ Associate Professor of Practice, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref: 26/78/HS/ACAD) Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/ or sub-degree levels in the following areas: Clinical Biology Community/ Primary Health Health Care Health Sciences Human Biology Nursing Studies Pharmaceutical Dispensing Appointment Criteria Applicants should have an earned and recognised Doctoral degree in relevant disciplines.  Preference will be given to those with teaching experience in degree / higher diploma programmes. A good command of English and Chinese is required. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time / Part-time Associate Professors / Assistant Professors / Senior Lecturers , Rita Tong Liu School of Business and Hospitality Management (Ref: 26/81/BHM/ACAD) Digital Marketing Marketing in Social Media Services Marketing Sales Management Hotel Operations & Management Accounting Hong Kong Taxation Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at sub-degree, undergraduate, and/or postgraduate levels in more than one subject area, including AI and ESG-related topics. Additionally, the appointee will undertake scholarly/research activities and programme/course administration. Appointment Criteria For Assistant Professor, applicants should have (a) a PhD or other recognised doctoral degree in a relevant discipline; and (b) relevant teaching/professional experience. Preference will be given to those who have a good record in teaching undergraduate and/or postgraduate programmes, especially with experience in AI applications for teaching and assessments, also experience in programme management and accreditation, and a proven research record. Applicants may be considered for the rank of Associate Professor or above depending on research record, experience, and qualifications. For Senior Lecturer, a Master's degree and professional membership in Hong Kong or overseas will be considered as appropriate for the particular disciplines. A good command of English is required and proficiency in Chinese (Putonghua) is preferable. In addition to the above, applicants should have at least three years of supervisory or managerial industry experience. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled [Full-time/ Part-time] Associate Professor / Assistant Professor/ Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer, Yam Pak Charitable Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences  (Ref: 26/71/CIS/ACAD) Deep Learning/ Artificial Intelligence Applications / Multimedia/ Computer Vision / AI interdisciplinary with other areas The School of Computing and Information Sciences ( https://cis.sfu.edu.hk/ ) at Saint Francis University is setting up a distributed/federated learning laboratory and is expanding its research and educational programmes in Artificial Intelligence and in Creative Media as a newly established Catholic University in Hong Kong, Saint Francis University. It also aims at strengthening the research culture in useful and high-impact technology area to better enable its faculty members to coach the students to become professionals in dream jobs in these fields. Candidates with background on interdisciplinarity between Artificial Intelligence and other areas including but not limited to design, healthcare, education, language are also needed. There are positions at different levels, including both full-time and part-time. Duties Undertake teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; Undertake duties in course/ programme/ curriculum review and development; Conduct research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; Engage in high-level consultancy, and other scholarly activities; Perform academic and administrative duties; and Perform any other Responsibilities and Tasks as assigned by the Dean of School or his delegate. Appointment Criteria For Assistant Professor, applicants should have (a) a PhD or other recognised doctoral degree in a relevant discipline; and (b) substantial relevant research/ teaching/ industrial experience. Preference will be given to those who have a good record in teaching undergraduate and/or postgraduate programmes, experience in programme management and accreditation, and a proven research record. Applicants may be considered for the rank of Associate Professor or above depending on research record, experience, and qualifications. For Senior Lecturer / Lecturer, a recognised Master degree in relevant disciplines; and (ii) substantial relevant research/ teaching/ industrial experience. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Professors/ Senior Lecturers/ Lecturers, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences  (Ref: 26/61/HS/ACAD) Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/ or sub-degree levels in the following areas: Health Care / Sciences Nursing Studies Pharmaceutical Dispensing Appointment Criteria Applicants should have an earned and recognised Master's degree in relevant disciplines. Preference will be given to those with Doctoral degree and teaching experience in degree / higher diploma programmes. A good command of English and Chinese is required. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time/ Part-time Assistant Professors / Senior Lecturers / Lecturers, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref: 26/35/SS/ACAD) Community Studies Psychology Social Care Social Work Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/or sub-degree levels in related areas. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a recognised Master degree in relevant disciplines; and (ii) relevant teaching / professional experience. Preference will be given to those with doctoral degree having teaching experience in degree programmes/ proven research record. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Professors / Senior Lecturers / Lecturers, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref: 26/34/HL/ACAD) English Language and English Literature (Academic English courses, English Communication, etc.) Chinese Language and Chinese Literature Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/ or sub-degree levels in related areas. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) an earned and recognised Doctoral degree in relevant disciplines (Master's degree holders will be considered for the post at Lecturer grade); and (ii) relevant teaching/ professional experience.  Preference will be given to those with experience in curriculum design, programme development and management. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required as appropriate for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled [Full-time/Part-time] Professors / Associate Professors, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref: 25/58/SS/ACAD) Duties Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences Community Studies Psychology Social Care Social Work The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/or sub-degree levels in related areas. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a recognised Doctoral degree in relevant disciplines; and (ii) relevant teaching / professional experience. Preference will be given to those with teaching experience in degree programmes/ proven research record. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the position is filled 新界将军澳翠岭里2号（港铁调景岭站B出口） (852) 3702 4388 (852) 3653 6798 info@sfu.edu.hk 网站地图 关于方大 校长欢迎辞 圣方济各大学概览 大学管治 大学管理 大学刊物 学院 行政部门 入学申请 为何选择SFU 开办课程 - 按学院分类 开办课程 - 按资历级别分类 入学申请 入学申请系统 招生热线 奖学金、助学金及经济援助 常见问题 课程注册 学