w Programme Admissions 2025/26 Programme List Apply Now JUPAS E-APP About SFU Home About SFU Academic Schools Caritas Bianchi College of Careers - Irene Lam Department of Design President's Message Expand Biography of the President Overview of the University Expand Motto, Vision and Mission Milestones Campus Environment and Facilities Governance Expand Board of Governors Council Management Expand University Administration Heads of Administrative and Learning Support Units Organisational Chart Strategic Plan Publications Expand Annual Report Quality Assurance Handbook University Newsletter Research Reports Academic Schools Expand Rita Tong Liu School of Business and Hospitality Management Yam Pak Charitable Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences Caritas Bianchi College of Careers - Irene Lam Department of Design Caritas Bianchi College of Careers - Faith Hope Love Department of General Education Non-Academic Units Expand Career Centre Centre for Advanced and Professional Studies Centre for Excellence Chaplaincy Finance and Estates Office Love-Learn-Inherit Institutional Advancement Office Global and Mainland Engagement Division Industry University Partnerships Office Information Technology Services Centre University Secretariat Physiotherapy Integrated Clinical Education Centre Language Centre Library Planning Office Public Affairs Office Quality Assurance Office Registry Student Affairs Office Introduction Department of Design has been providing quality design programmes for the community since 1971 which offers a substantial portfolio of courses that has been proven to be well accepted and recognised by its stakeholders. We believe that education plays a pivotal role in the society as it influences the supply and quality of innovation, and that innovation should be non-exclusive and design should be an indispensable and integrated process for any task in any industry and society. We believe that our programmes should offers a balanced development in the domains of professional knowledge, language proficiency, and general social skills which can bring students to an all-round, balanced, coherent learning life, prospective careers and future education potentials. The Department of Design distinguishes itself by cherishing the close teacher-student relationship in the studio-based learning environment. We emphasis on offering students a broad range of learning experiences with an interdisciplinary approach stressing on innovation that exemplifies the understanding of aesthetics, technology, business, and human values. A vital integrative environment is created within the Department where students and academic staff across the design disciplines can share and exchange diverse ideas and design experiences. We aspire to cultivate our students and to distinguish them from graduates of other institutes with the following qualities: Multidisciplinary Knowledge Industry-readiness / Professionalism Cultural and Global Awareness Social Responsibility Sub-Menu Introduction Head’s Message Programmes Offerings 2 Chui Ling Lane, Tseung Kwan O (Exit B, Tiu Keng Leng MTR Station), New Territories (852) 3702 4388 (852) 3653 6798 info@sfu.edu.hk Sitemap About SFU President's Message Overview of the University Governance Management Publications Academic Schools Non-Academic Units Admissions Why SFU Programmes by School Programmes by QF Level Admissions Admissions Portal Admission Hotlines Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance Admissions FAQ Programme Registration Student Support & Services Useful Information Services Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance College Life Useful Links Research Funded Projects Research Experts Research Highlights Research Office Research Centres and Laboratories Giving Home About Us Welcome Message Shatin Campus Development News & Event Research Matching Grant Scheme SFU Campus Acknowledgement Opportunities Give Now Our Donors Contact Us Global and Mainland Affairs About GMED Mainland Affairs Engagement Global Affairs Engagement Events and Activities News SFU Cultural Ambassabor Programme Sharing Students Staff Alumni Media Visitors Library Career Admissions Hotlines Site Map Privacy Statement Copyright © 2026 Saint Francis University. All Rights Reserved."
