lery University titling: FAQ for Alumni Media Press Release Media Coverage Latest Updates Recruitment and Outreach SFU Photo Gallery Media Enquiry Visitors Getting to Campus Campus Map Campus Environment and Facilities Library Career Senior Management Positions Deanship / Headship Positions Academic / Teaching Positions Administrative / Services Positions Research / Project Positions Internal Advertisement Admissions Hotlines Eng ENG 繁體 简體 About SFU President's Message Overview of the University Governance Management Publications Academic Schools Non-Academic Units Admissions Why SFU Programmes by School Programmes by QF Level Admissions Admissions Portal Admission Hotlines Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance Admissions FAQ Programme Registration Student Support & Services Useful Information Expand Forms Download Academic Calendar Handbook Bad Weather Arrangements Moodle (Web Learning Platform) Services Expand Library Services IT Services Career Services Counselling Service Language Centre Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance Expand Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance JUPAS Programme Scholarships Admission Scholarships Internal Articulation Scholarships Programme Scholarships Other Scholarships Bursaries and Financial Assistance College Life Expand Campus Facilities Room Booking Off-campus Student Accommodation Students Activities and Training Programmes Life Education Student Groups Useful Links Expand Student Support Services Student Email System Moodle (Web Learning Platform) Room Booking JUPAS SSSDP E-APP Research Funded Projects Research Experts Research Highlights Research Office Research Centres and Laboratories Giving Home About Us Welcome Message Shatin Campus Development News & Event Research Matching Grant Scheme SFU Campus Acknowledgement Opportunities Give Now Our Donors Contact Us Global and Mainland Affairs About GMED Mainland Affairs Engagement Global Affairs Engagement Events and Activities News SFU Cultural Ambassabor Programme Sharing Apply Now Programme Admissions 2025/26 Programme List Apply Now JUPAS E-APP Career Home Career Deanship / Headship Positions Senior Management Positions Deanship / Headship Positions Academic / Teaching Positions Administrative / Services Positions Research / Project Positions Internal Advertisement Notes For Applicants: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested parties are invited to submit: a written application indicating expected salary; a CV; and a duly completed application form . Please email to hrm@sfu.edu.hk before the application deadline. Candidates not invited for interview within 2 months after the application deadline may assume their applications unsuccessful. Download Application Form here All personal data provided by the applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used only for recruitment and employment-related purposes. Deanship / Headship Positions Director of Finance & Estates Office (Ref.: 26/90/FEO/D) Duties Lead and manage the FEO, ensuring efficient delivery of core operational functions including budgeting and financial planning, financial accounting, income collection and recording, payment processing, procurement and purchase requisitions, resource allocation, property and estate management, and general office administration. Provide strategic direction for financial planning and resource management, aligning resource allocation with university priorities and long-term objectives. Ensure the integrity of financial reporting and compliance with applicable accounting standards, statutory requirements and internal controls. Oversee income collection procedures to maximise revenue accuracy and timeliness. Lead procurement and payments processes, implementing best practices to ensure compliance with the financial management policies and maintaining appropriate controls. Oversee the University's property management and estate functions, monitoring the Property Management Office as well as external contractors and service providers to ensure standards and regulatory compliance. Develop, review and maintain robust policies, guidelines and procedures across finance, procurement, resource allocation and estates management to promote good governance and operational efficiency. Prepare proposals, project planning, budgets and other necessary documentation for campus development and capital projects; and coordinate with internal and external stakeholders as required. Lead or contribute to major capital project governance, including budget oversight, financial modelling, risk assessment and reporting. Provide advice to senior leadership on financial implications of strategic initiatives and campus development options. Mentor, develop and build capacity within the FEO team to ensure high performance and succession planning. Undertake ad hoc assignments and special projects as requested by the Vice-President (Finance & Institutional Advancement). Appointment Criteria Applicants should meet the following criteria: Possess a recognized master's degree or above level in accounting, finance, business administration, or a related discipline; Possess a professional accounting qualification (e.g. HKCPA); Possess significant post-qualification experience in senior finance, estates or resources management roles, preferably within higher education, the public sector or large organisations; Possess substantive knowledge of financial management, budgeting, accounting standards and procurement practices; Have demonstrated experience in managing capital or campus development projects, including preparation of business cases and financial models; Have excellent leadership and people management skills, with proven experience building and leading multidisciplinary teams; Have strong stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to liaise effectively with academic and administrative leaders, external consultants and regulatory bodies; and Have high integrity, sound judgement and a strong commitment to good governance. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Director of Student Affairs (Ref.: 26/75/SAO/D) Duties The Director of Student Affairs will assist the University in formulating, implementing and reviewing systems, strategies and plans for student development and support. The appointee will head the Student Affairs Office with a team of professional staff and oversee the provision of co-curriculum including whole-person development, service learning, sport development, global exposure, counseling, support for non-local and SEN students, career planning and guidance, alumni affairs etc… He/ She is also expected to act as a liaison person between students and the University, and work closely with academic schools/ departments, administrative units and student groups to cultivate a campus environment conductive to teaching, learning, campus life and wellness. Appointment Criteria Good academic and professional qualifications, preferably at a post-graduate degree level; Proven track record of management experience and serving youth in the tertiary education setting; Excellent communication, interpersonal, problem solving and negotiation skills; and Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled 2 Chui Ling Lane, Tseung Kwan O (Exit B, Tiu Keng Leng MTR Station), New Territories (852) 3702 4388 (852) 3653 6798 info@sfu.edu.hk Sitemap About SFU President's Message Overview of the University Governance Management Publications Academic Schools Non-Academic Units Admissions Why SFU Programmes by School Programmes by QF Level Admissions Admissions Portal Admission Hotlines Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance Admissions FAQ Programme Registration Student Support & Services Useful Information Services Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance College Life Useful Links Research Funded Projects Research Experts Research High