Cultural Ambassabor Programme Sharing Apply Now Programme Admissions 2025/26 Programme List Apply Now JUPAS E-APP Career Home Career Administrative / Services Positions Senior Management Positions Deanship / Headship Positions Academic / Teaching Positions Administrative / Services Positions Research / Project Positions Internal Advertisement Notes For Applicants: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested parties are invited to submit: a written application indicating expected salary; a CV; and a duly completed application form Please email to: hrm@sfu.edu.hk before the application deadline. Candidates not invited for interview within 2 months after the application deadline may assume their applications unsuccessful. Download Application Form here All personal data provided by the applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used only for recruitment and employment-related purposes. Administrative / Services Positions Assistant Registrar, Registry (Ref.: 26/117/REG/AR) Duties Reporting to the Registrar, the appointee will be responsible for (a) assisting the Registrar in providing strategic leadership and direction for Registry operations and academic administration; (b) overseeing designated functional areas within the Registry and ensuring the effective management of staff, resources, and service delivery; (c) spearheading the digital transformation of Registry services through the development, implementation, and continuous enhancement of administrative systems, workflow automation, and technology-enabled solutions; (d) reviewing and optimizing business processes, policies, and procedures to enhance operational effectiveness and service excellence; (e) overseeing the administration of academic regulations, student records, examinations, graduation, quality assurance, and other Registry-related functions as assigned; (f) preparing institutional reports, statistical analyses, and management information to support governance and strategic planning; (g) fostering effective collaboration with internal and external stakeholders to ensure the successful implementation of policies, systems, and projects; (h) supporting committee work and providing professional advice on academic administration, governance, and regulatory matters; (i) leading special projects and initiatives to support the University's strategic development; and (j) performing any other duties as assigned by the Registrar. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (a) hold a Bachelor's degree, preferably a Master's degree, with a minimum of 15 years of relevant full-time post-qualification experience, including at least 5 years in a leadership role within a higher education setting; (b) demonstrate a strong IT and system development background, with proven experience in leading or participating in the development, enhancement, implementation, and optimization of administrative systems and digital solutions to improve operational efficiency, service delivery, and business processes; (c) demonstrate strong organizational and interpersonal skills; (d) possess excellent communication abilities with a high level of proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese; (e) exhibit a proven capacity to work independently and efficiently under tight deadlines, while managing multiple tasks in an organized manner; (f) demonstrate effective teamwork skills, be self-motivated, and capable of performing well under pressure; and (g) preferably have experience working in the Registry of local self-financing tertiary education institutions. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Library Officer (Access Services), Library (Ref.: 26/113/LIB/ALO) Duties The appointee will be required to (1) discharge operational duties relating to circulation services, information enquiries, shelving, collections and facilities maintenance; (2) provide technical and administrative support and collate statistical data on the circulation of library materials; (3) assist in managing course readings; (4) offer assistance to library patrons in the use of services and facilities; (5) help with the supervision of part-time Library Assistants; (6) work at service counters on a shift basis, including at evenings and on weekends; and (7) carry out other duties as assigned by the supervisors or the University Librarian. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (1) a recognized Degree or Higher Diploma, preferably in library information management related disciplines; (2) a familiarity with the academic library systems and discovery services; (3) experience in providing circulation and information services in an academic library setting; (4) a reasonably high level of proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); and (5) an ability to work independently and/ or within a team and to perform duties in a self-motivated, collegial and responsible manner. Fresh graduates are welcome to apply, but preference will be given to applicants who are conversant with academic library operations. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Library Officer (Acquisitions), Library (Ref.: 26/112/LIB/ALO) Duties The appointee will be required to (1) assist in the acquisition of library materials in both print and electronic formats, undertaking tasks including placing and receiving orders as well as handling payment transactions; (2) provide technical and administrative support, and compile statistical data related to acquisitions; (3) discharge operational duties relating to circulation services, information enquiries, shelving and collections maintenance; (4) work at service counters on a shift basis, including at evenings and on weekends; and (5) carry out other duties as assigned by the supervisors or the University Librarian. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (1) a recognized Degree or Higher Diploma, preferably in library information management related disciplines; (2) a familiarity with the academic library systems and discovery services; (3) a reasonably high level of proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (4) an ability to work independently and/ or within a team and to perform duties in a self-motivated, collegial and responsible manner. Fresh graduates are welcome to apply, but preference will be given to applicants who are conversant with academic library operations. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Public Affairs Officer (Communications), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/108/PAO/PAO) Duties The appointee will be required to: Draft, edit and coordinate press releases, speeches, newspaper op-eds, brochures, newsletters, annual reports and other communications materials in both English and Chinese; Identify and develop newsworthy stories about the University's achievements, initiatives and people, and assist in pitching them to the media; Assist in maintaining media relations and responding to media enquiries; Monitor and analyse media coverage, and prepare regular reports on media sentiment and public perception of the University; Assist in organising media visits, publicity events, stakeholder engagement and community outreach programmes; Support the implementation of the Public Affairs Office's corporate communications, branding and publicity strategies; Maintain media lists, communications records and relevant databases; and Perform any other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess: A recognised degree, preferably in journalism, communications, marketing, public relations or a related discipline; At least three years of relevant working experience in communications, public relations, marketing or a related field; Experience in news media or media relations will be a definite advantage; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; Strong writing, editing and interpersonal skills; Proficiency in word processing, presentation software, digital communications tools and AI applications; The ability to work effectively with different stakeholders and manage multiple tasks under tight deadlines; and Good organisational and project coordination skills. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Project Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences   (Ref.: 26/107/HS/PA) Duties To support the administrative work and deployment of the project To assist in handling documents and promotional materials arising from the project, including the progress report To coordinate and assist in the implementation of the system in the hosting institution To coordinate the promotion, training and sharing session of the system to students and academic staff in the hosting institution To assist in collecting user experience feedback surveys To serve as the contact person of Saint Francis University (SFU) to liaise with the project team members, academics, clinical experts, service providers and vendors in facilitating and developing the scenarios, software and hardware facilities Appointment Criteria A Bachelor's degree in Health, Education, Psychology or Computing Sciences or related discipline, or equivalent qualification Have a strong sense of responsibility and self-motivation Good command of English and Chinese is an advantage Good organizational and interpersonal skills with cultural sensitivity Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Senior Laboratory Technician, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences  (Ref.: 26/106/HS/SLT) Duties Assist supervisor of the nursing faculty to implement the skills laboratory curriculum. This includes the use of a variety of patient care equipment and supplies. Assist supervisor in developing the system to ensure all laboratory equipment is properly maintained and functioning in relation to manufacturer's recommendations. Function as a team head for laboratory technicians to deliver efficient support for the daily operation of nurse labs. Organize nursing