ation, the public sector or large organisations; Strong knowledge of financial management, budgeting, accounting standards and procurement practices; Experience in handling project accounts and financial monitoring; Good analytical skills with the ability to interpret financial data and identity key issues; Strong attention to detail and high level of accuracy in financial work; and Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Public Affairs Officer (Marketing), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/88/PAO/O) Duties The Public Affairs Office (PAO) is seeking a creative and digitally savvy individual to support its marketing and communications initiatives. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Public Affairs, the appointee will be primarily responsible for: Executing social media and content marketing initiatives to enhance the University's digital presence, drive engagement, and support broader branding and marketing objectives; Creating high-quality written, visual, and multimedia content for online and offline platforms, and managing digital and social media channels such as LinkedIn, Instagram, WeChat, RedNote, and Facebook; Producing high quality marketing collateral, event and promotional materials; Attending events and activities to capture content, including photography, video, and real-time social media updates, for promotional use; Work closely with internal teams and stakeholders to ensure content and campaigns are aligned with the University's branding, messaging, and communication priorities; Coordinating with external service providers for digital campaigns, targeted advertising, SEO/ SEM, and social media support; Supporting the University's offline branding and marketing events and activities; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria A recognised degree, preferably in Marketing, Communications, Journalism,