ltiple channels, including the University website, paid search, paid social, display advertising, and content marketing; Developing organic content (including social media posts, visuals, photography, and videos) and managing official social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, WeChat and RedNote to drive branding and student recruitment efforts; Working closely with internal stakeholders, external agencies, and partners to implement promotional initiatives and achieve defined KPIs; Driving performance monitoring and analytics, including website traffic, campaign effectiveness, and competitor benchmarking, and providing strategic insights and recommendations to inform continuous improvement; Supporting the University's offline branding and marketing events and activities; Monitoring social media trends, platform developments, and online community sentiment, and supporting the identification and mitigation of potential reputational risks in collaboration with the communication team; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria A recognised degree, preferably in Marketing, Business, Journalism, Communications, Public Relations, or a related discipline; 8 -15 years of solid experience in branding and digital marketing, with a proven track record in social media strategy, content development, performance marketing, analytics, and lead generation; Demonstrated success in developing and driving integrated, omni-channel marketing strategies, including SEO/ SEM, social media growth, paid advertising, and delivering measurable outcomes; Strong practical knowledge of key digital platforms and Martech tools, including Google Ads, Google Analytics, Meta Ads, and related solutions; A strategic and analytical mindset, with the ability to interpret complex data, derive insights, and translate them into effective marketing strategies and business impact; Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; proficiency in Putonghua is an advantage; Hands-on skills in design and video production tools (e.g. Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro or equivalent) would be an advantage; A mature, self-driven professional with strong sense of ownership, attention to detail, and a solutions-oriented approach; Proven ability to lead and collaborate effectively within small, agile teams, with strong interpersonal and stakeholder management skills; Highly organised, with strong project management, prioritisation, and time management capabilities; Ability to manage multiple initiatives independently in a fast-paced environment, while maintaining quality under tight timelines; and Flexible and willing to work outside office hours when necessary. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Manager (Marketing), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/86/PAO/AM) Duties The Public Affairs Office (PAO) is seeking a dynamic individual to support its marketing and communications initiatives. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Public Affairs, the appointee will be primarily responsible for: Supporting the development of branding and marketing strategies, and executing integrated full-funnel campaigns to strengthen the University's visibility and market positioning; Planning and implementing data-informed digital marketing campaigns across multiple channels, including the University website, paid search, paid social, display advertising, and content marketing; Creating and managing organic content (including social media posts, visuals, photography, and videos) and overseeing official social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, WeChat and RedNote to support branding and student recruitment; Coordinating with internal stakeholders, external agencies, and partners to deliver promotional initiatives and achieve defined KPIs; Monitoring and analysing campaign performance, including website traffic, campaign effectiveness, and competitor activities, and preparing regular reports with actio