ree/ Degree in any discipline; (b) have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (c) be competent in computing application, (d) possess good communication skills with a pleasant, polite, and friendly personality; (e) be a good team player with a strong sense of responsibility; and (f) have 1 year's relevant work experience (preferable). Candidates with more experience may be considered for the post of Executive Assistant I. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Manager (Student Recruitment and Engagement Team), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/36/PAO/AM) Duties The successful candidate will be responsible for implementing strategic initiatives to enhance the School's engagement with external stakeholders, including feeder schools, prospective students, alumni, university partners, and the broader community. The appointee will support the Assistant Director, Recruitment and Engagement at the Public Affairs Office in leading admissions and partnership development for the local market. The appointee will lead recruitment and partnership initiatives to strengthen collaboration between the University and Hong Kong Secondary Schools, including organising information sessions for principals and teachers, conducting school visits to enhance recruitment, and hosting networking events for external stakeholders. The appointee will also build and maintain strong relationships with targeted feeder schools and partner organisations to expand the School's network and influence, and will identify and pursue strategic partnership opportunities, such as drafting and managing Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs). This is a KPI driven role. The role also includes planning and overseeing events such as conferences, exchange programmes, and stakeholder engagement activities. Key responsibilities: Support the development and implementation of external relations and stakeholder engagement plans to enhance the School's reputation and increase student recruitment. Identify and build relationships with key stakeholders, including secondary schools in Hong Kong, prospective students, alumni, university partners, and government authorities. Assist in planning, executing, and coordinating stakeholder engagement events and activities, such as conferences, ceremonies, and visits. Devise and implement stakeholder engagement plans to strengthen stakeholder relations, foster a close-knit SFU community, and support the ongoing expansion of the SFU profile other duties as assigned by the Assistant Director (Recruitment and Engagement). Appointment Criteria Applicants must possess a bachelor's degree, preferably in a business-related discipline, and have at least three years of relevant post-qualification experience in a higher education institution. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong problem-solving abilities, an outgoing disposition, the capacity to work independently and collaboratively, meticulous attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks under strict deadlines. Candidates should be self-motivated, effective team players, and exhibit strong interpersonal, communication, and coordination skills. Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese is essential. Occasional work outside regular office hours, including weekends, public holidays, or evenings, may be required. The appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time/ Part-time Laboratory Technician, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/13/HS/LT) Duties Provide support for teaching, research and service to the School of Health Sciences in the nursing and other health-care courses. Follow school directions for nursing skills laboratory station set-up and aftercare of supplies/equipment in all teaching, skills assessment and students' self-practice Assist in the setting up, operation and maintenance of the equipment required for teaching / learning activities including manikins, simulation models, patient-care equipment and other computing / audio visual facilities. Maintain inventory of laboratory equipment and supplies to ensure equipment are in good condition and supplies are adequate. Maintain the daily operation of the nursing skills laboratories and ensure a safe and clean condition in all work areas. Assist in-house and vendor servicing of laboratory equipment, follow any required repairs / maintenance and to keep updated records for tracking. Support and facilitate the student self-practice sessions in the nursing skills laboratories. Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of the School of Health Sciences or his delegates. The appointee may be required to work outside normal office hours and on Saturdays and Sundays due to specific operational requirement. Appointment Criteria Five passes in HKCEE/HKDSE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics. Good computer knowledge and experience in using application software such as MS Office, photo/video editing software and e-learning system, etc. Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese. Good communication, interpersonal and organizational skills; and able to work independently. Preferred Attributes / Exposure Working experience in health care institution Holding certificate of health care related study Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/07/HS/AA) Duties The appointee will be responsible for Providing administrative support to academic programmes and general office management; Assist in organising departmental events, student activities and academic visits; Compile records and maintain databases; Handle enquiries from students and external parties; and Performing other tasks as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have Achieved Level 2 or above in five subjects in the HKDSE, or have obtained Grade E or above in five subjects in the HKCEE; Proficiency in MS Office, including Word and Excel; A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; Good organisational and communication skills; and Preferably with 1-2 year's relevant work experience. Those with lower qualifications may be considered for the post of Administrative Assistant II. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled 2 Chui Ling Lane, Tseung Kwan O (Exit B, Tiu Keng Leng MTR Station), New Territories (852) 3702 4388 (852) 3653 6798 info@sfu.edu.hk Sitemap About SFU President's Message Overview of the University Governance Management Publications Academic Schools Non-Academic Units Admissions Why SFU Programmes by School Programmes by QF Level Admissions Admissions Portal Admission Hotlines Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance Admissions FAQ Programme Registration Student Support & Services Useful Information Services Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance College Life Useful Links Research Funded Projects Research Experts Research Highlights Research Office Research Centres and Laboratories Giving Home About Us Welcome Message Shatin Campus Development News & Event Research Matching Grant Scheme SFU Campus Acknowledgement Opportunities Give Now Our Donors Contact Us Global and Mainland Affairs About GMED Mainland Affairs Engagement Global Affairs Engagement Events and Activities News SFU Cultural Ambassabor Programme Sharing Students Staff Alumni Media Visitors Library Career Admissions Hotlines Moodle Site Map Privacy Statement Copyright © 2026 Saint Francis University. All Rights Reserved."
