sabor Programme Sharing Apply Now Programme Admissions 2025/26 Programme List Apply Now JUPAS E-APP Career Home Career Research / Project Positions Senior Management Positions Deanship / Headship Positions Academic / Teaching Positions Administrative / Services Positions Research / Project Positions Internal Advertisement Notes For Applicants: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested parties are invited to submit: a written application indicating expected salary; a CV; and a duly completed application form Please email to hrm@sfu.edu.hk before the application deadline. Candidates not invited for interview within 2 months after the application deadline may assume their applications unsuccessful. Download Application Form here All personal data provided by the applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used only for recruitment and employment-related purposes. Research / Project Positions Senior Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/115/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator and Co-Principal Investigators under Caregiving Research and Development Centre. His/her task will include (i) assisting in the preparation of research proposals, funding applications, ethics submissions and project reports; (ii) conducting literature reviews, designing research instruments and coordinating research projects; (iii) conducting qualitative and quantitative data collection and analysis using software such as NVivo and SPSS; (iv) arranging and conducting interviews and focus groups, as well as designing survey questionnaires; (v) drafting research manuscripts and presentation materials for conferences and journals; (vi) assisting in the development of operational manuals, training materials and reports; (vii) supporting event planning and project-related activities; and (viii) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's degree, preferably with a Master's/MPhil degree in Social Sciences or a related discipline; (ii) solid training and experience in research methods and data analysis, both quantitative and qualitative; (iii) demonstrated experience in preparing research proposals, funding applications, research reports and academic manuscripts; (iv) excellent English and Chinese proficiency; (v) a minimum of two years of relevant experience in research project coordination, data analysis, research report writing and/or academic publication. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/114/HL/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project on: (a) administrative and coordinating work (b) collecting data and pre-processing them for experiments; (c) recruiting participants in experiments; (d) annotating data; (e) managing and updating datasets; (f) preparing reports; and (g) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized Bachelor's degree in humanities field; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken Chinese and English; and (f) proficiency in computer applications. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/110/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will support the Principal Investigator in a research project aimed at \"Development and evaluation of a Chatbot to Enhance Clinical Learning in Nursing Students\". The appointee will be responsible to assist administrative and coordinating work for the research project. Tasks include: (a) arranging the research study; (b) collecting data and conducting data analysis; (c) preparing reports; (d) organizing seminars and workshops; (d) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (i) have a recognised Bachelor's Degree; (ii) have relevant research experience in the handling of data entry, transcription and utilizing SPSS software analysis; (iii) be able to work independently, attention to detail with positive working attitude; and (iv) have good communication skills and fluency in English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/101/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) in a research project aimed how capitals affect students' engagement with GenAI tools and their academic performance on: (a) review and conduct literature review; (b) recruiting participants; (c) perform quantitative data analysis (d) prepare materials for conference presentations and publications; (e) handle relevant administrative tasks; (f) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized bachelor's degree or above in social sciences or a related discipline, preferably in the area of Psychology and/or Sociology; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude, responsible, self-motivated and ability to work independently; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English; (f) proficiency in using analytical tools (e.g., SPSS or R). Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Senior Research Assistant, Graduate School (Ref.: 26/100/GS/RA) Duties The appointee is mainly required to assist in an innovative research project entitled ' An Integrative Psychosocial Study and Service Outcome Evaluation for Students with Special Educational Needs . The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator, the Co-investigators and the team in conducting the research tasks, including: (a) reviewing literature; (b) conducting large-scale mixed-method research; (c) coordinating with research team members and collaborating partners; (d) collecting and analyzing quantitative and qualitative data; (e) conducting in-depth interviews; (f) compiling research reports and high-impact peer-reviewed journal articles; (g) supervising research assistants, and (h) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants for Senior Research Assistant should (i) have a recognised Master's degree or above in Social Sciences / Applied Psychology / Statistics / Computer or Data Science; (ii) with at least five years of relevant research experience in quantitative and qualitative research methods, a track record of publications will be considered an advantage; (iii) familiar with procedures of research adopting randomized controlled trial and/or mixed-methods; (iv) have knowledge in data analytic software, including SPSS and NVivo, knowledge in Statistical modeling will be considered an advantage; (v) able to work independently, have an investigative nature and an analytical aptitude, attention to detail, ability to synthesize research into clear, compelling outputs; and (vi) have good communication skills and fluency in English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences  (Ref.: 26/99/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will support a project that aims to explore nurses' perspectives on promoting advanced directives and assess their capacity to manage end-of-life care and related issues. Responsibilities include (a) coordinating activities, (b) collecting and analyzing both quantitative and qualitative data, (c) reviewing the relevant literature, (d) providing administrative support, (e) assisting the research team in preparing research reports, and (f) performing any other duties assigned by the project leader. Appointment Criteria Applicants must meet the following criteria: (i) possess a recognized Master's degree in statistics, health sciences, or a related field; (ii) have at five years of relevant post-qualification experience; (iii) demonstrate a strong command of both written and spoken Chinese and English; and (iv) exhibit proficiency in SPSS, along with experience in both quantitative and qualitative data collection and analysis. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time / Part-time Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/97/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will support the Principal Investigator in a research project aimed at collecting data from South Asian communities. Irregular working hours and/or weekend work may be required, particularly for data collection The appointee will be responsible to: conduct literature review; recruit research participants and conduct in-depth interviews; perform qualitative data analysis and compile research reports; prepare materials for conference presentations and publications; handle relevant administrative tasks; perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should: have a recognized bachelor degree or above in social sciences or relevant disciplines; have at least one year of relevant work experience; have a good network within South Asian communities; be familiar with procedures for conducting in-depth interviews; possess knowledge and skills in qualitative data analysis; have good communication, organizational and interpersonal skills; be responsible, self-motivated and able to work independently; have an excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/91/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will be responsible to assist staff members within the School to conduct administrative and coordinating research activities and research projects. Tasks include: (a) literature search, (b) coordinating research work, (c) collecting data and conducting data analysis; (d) preparing reports; and (e) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) at least a bachelor's degree in nursing, health science, allied health backgrounds, or statistics-related qualifications; (ii) 3-4 years of research experience and knowledge of quantitative research, and prior experience of conducting statistical analysis are preferred. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Project Officer, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/85/HL/PO) Duties The appointees will (a) assist the work of system construction and maintenance of the project; (b) help with the teaching of computer-related courses of the programmes of the School; and (c) perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a bachelor's degree or master's degree in computer science or relevant fields; (b) familiarity with database management tools (such as SQL, MS Access, etc.); (c) knowledge and skills of programming (such as Python); (d) proficiency in image technology; and (e) able to work independently. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Yam Pak Charitable Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/84/CIS/RA) We are seeking a self-motivated, capable, and research-oriented individual to join our team as a Research Assistant for the RGC-funded project: \"Harnessing Large Language Models for Social Trust: Automated Fact-checking for Public Health Informatics by Large Language Models\" Project No.: UGC/FDS11/E05/25 This position is particularly suitable for applicants who wish to strengthen their research profile, gain hands-on experience in AI and large language model (LLM) applications, and contribute to publishable research outputs. The project focuses on the application of LLMs to automated fact-checking, public health informatics, misinformation detection, and social trust. Applicants with relevant experience or a strong interest in LLMs, AI applications, NLP, data analytics, or research publication are highly encouraged to apply. Duties The appointee will be responsible for supporting the project team in conducting research related to LLMs. Major duties include assisting in literature review, data collection and analysis, experiment design and implementation, result interpretation, manuscript preparation, and publication of research findings in scientific journals and conferences. The appointee is also expected to complete other research-related tasks assigned by the Project Leader. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess: A Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline; The ability to work independently and responsibly; Good communication and interpersonal skills; Good English writing skills; and A strong interest in research, AI, LLMs, NLP, or data-driven applications. Applicants with prior research experience, publication experience, programming skills, or hands-on experience with LLMs will be given priority. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filledl Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/80/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project on \"Mental health literacy, psychological well-being and healthy ageing perceptions of community-based older adults with low to mild distress in Hong Kong: A mixed methods study\". The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator in: Recruitment of research participants from the community; Obtaining consent documents and data collection including administering surveys; Conducting semi-structured interviews and transcribing audio recordings; Performing basic quantitative data analysis using SPSS and preliminary qualitative thematic analysis; Working mainly in SFU and visiting NGO centres (if required); and Performing any other duties as assigned by PI. Appointment Criteria A recognized bachelor's degree or above in Nursing, health science or a related discipline; 1-2 years of research experience and knowledge of quantitative and qualitative research; Prior experience of conducting statistical analysis and thematic analysis; Have a good interpersonal and communication skills; and Be able to work independently. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/77/HL/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project \" The Importance of Disciplinary Literacy in iGCSE: A Data Driven Study in Hong Kong \" on: (a) administrative and coordinating work (b) collecting data and pre-processing them for data analysis; (c) recruiting school participants; (d) annotating data; (e) managing and updating datasets; (f) preparing reports; and (g) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized Bachelor's degree in humanities field, preferably in the area of English language education and/or linguistics; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English;  (f) proficiency in computer applications; and (g) corpus knowledge is preferable. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Graduate School (Ref.: 26/76/GS/RA) Duties The appointee is mainly required to assist in a 5-year innovative service-research project entitled 'Meta-S: An Integrative Psychosocial Study and Service Outcome Evaluation for Students with Special Educational Needs'. The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator, the Co-investigators, and the team in carrying out project-related tasks, including: (a) supporting the planning and coordination of project activities (e.g. seminars, workshops); (b) arranging and conducting research activities (e.g. surveys, in-depth interviews); (c) preparing and analyzing data derived from the project; (d) compiling research reports and publication; (e) handling relevant administrative tasks, and (f) performing other duties as assigned by the PI. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (i) have a recognized Bachelor's degree or above in Social Work / Social Sciences / Education / Applied Research / Applied Psychology / Statistics; (ii) have relevant project or event management / research experience; (iii) have knowledge of Special Educational Needs (SEN) / Neurodiversity (ND); (iv) be able to work independently, have an investigative nature, attention to detail, and an analytical aptitude; (v) have good teamwork and interpersonal skills; and (vi) have good communication skills and fluency in English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/72/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator in all research related activities, include arranging and conducting survey questionnaires, interviews & focus groups with parents; conducting data analysis of the quantitative data and qualitative verbatim transcription; assisting in drafting operational manuals, forms, templates and reports; drafting research manuscripts for presentation/publication in conferences/journals; performing other tasks as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's degree, preferably with a Master's/MPhil degree in Social Sciences or a related discipline; (ii) solid training and experience in research methods, using SPSS software; (iii) excellent English and Chinese proficiency Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/67/CIS/RA) Join a cutting-edge research initiative at Saint Francis University. The project, \"AI and IoT in Telehealth,\" lies at the intersection of modern healthcare and technological innovation. We aim to leverage Internet of Things (IoT) medical devices and Artificial Intelligence (AI) to revolutionize remote patient monitoring, improve clinical decision-making, and bridge the gap in accessible healthcare. We are seeking a driven, multidisciplinary Full-Time Research Assistant to bridge the gap between health sciences and advanced technology. You will play a pivotal role in designing, testing, and implementing AI-driven telehealth solutions and managing IoT data pipelines. Duties The appointee will be responsible (a) assist in the development, training, and deployment of AI/Machine Learning models tailored for healthcare data; (b) support the integration and testing of IoT biosensors and remote monitoring devices; (c) collect, clean, and analyze clinical and health-related datasets; (d) collaborate with clinical partners to ensure technical solutions align with real-world healthcare needs; (e) contribute to academic papers, research reports, and grant proposals; and (f) manage day-to-day project logistics and documentation. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's or Master's degree in a Health Science-related field (e.g., Biomedical Science, Health Informatics, Nursing, Public Health) with a strong quantitative background, OR a degree in Biomedical Engineering / Computer Science with a heavy emphasis on healthcare applications; (ii) strong programming skills in Python or R (experience with frameworks like PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Scikit-learn is highly preferred); (iii) solid understanding of Machine Learning, Deep Learning, or statistical modeling techniques; (iv) familiarity with IoT concepts, data acquisition, or sensor technology; (v) excellent written and verbal communication skills for cross-disciplinary collaboration (tech and health); (vi) prior experience in a research environment or writing academic literature; and (vii) strong problem-solving skills and a passion for digital health innovation. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/66/CIS/RA) Join an innovative, high-impact research initiative at Saint Francis University. The project, \"AI and IoT Monitoring of Construction Tower Cranes,\" focuses on enhancing smart city infrastructure and construction safety. By integrating Internet of Things (IoT) sensors with advanced Artificial Intelligence (AI), this project aims to enable real-time structural health monitoring, predictive maintenance, and anomaly detection for tower cranes on active construction sites. We are seeking a technically skilled, motivated Part-Time Research Assistant with an engineering background. In this role, you will help bridge the gap between structural/mechanical systems and intelligent data science, contributing directly to the deployment of IoT hardware and the development of AI algorithms. Duties The appointee will be responsible (a) develop, train, and test AI/Machine Learning models for anomaly detection and predictive analytics using sensor data; (b) assist in processing, cleaning, and managing time-series data streams from IoT sensors (e.g., accelerometers, strain gauges, tilt sensors); (c) support the configuration, calibration, and data acquisition setup for IoT monitoring hardware; (d) collaborate with the research team to validate AI model insights against real-world engineering constraints; and (e) assist in preparing technical reports, progress updates. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's or Master's degree (or currently enrolled in a postgraduate program) in Engineering (e.g., Civil, Mechanical, Electronic, Systems, or Biomedical Engineering with a strong structural/mechatronics focus); (ii) strong programming skills in Python or MATLAB (experience with libraries like NumPy, Pandas, TensorFlow, or PyTorch is highly preferred); (iii) solid understanding of Machine Learning, Deep Learning, or statistical signal processing; (iv) ability to interpret data related to structural mechanics, vibrations, or kinematics; (v) experience working with IoT hardware, microcontrollers (e.g., Arduino, Raspberry Pi), or edge computing, (vi) strong problem-solving abilities and a self-driven attitude toward research; and (vii) good written and verbal communication skills. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences  (Ref.: 26/65/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will be responsible to: conduct literature review perform data analysis and compile research reports prepare materials for conference presentations and publications perform other duties as assigned Appointment Criteria Applicants should: have a recognized bachelor degree or above in data sciences or relevant disciplines with proficiency in SPSS / Python / LLM and other computer software possess strong knowledge and skills in data analysis for project evaluations have good communication, organizational and interpersonal skills be responsible, self-motivated and able to work independently have an excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/64/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will play a key role in supporting a research project focused on \"Psychological\". Responsibilities include: Assisting in the management of the project; Coordinating with collaborative partners and project team; Providing support for the preparation of research material; Assisting in recruitment, data collection, data entry and data analysis; Conducting literature search; Assisting in the preparation of abstracts, manuscripts and reports; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the project leader or his/her delegates. Appointment Criteria Have a recognized degree or higher in Nursing, Social Sciences, Psychology or other related disciplines or an equivalent qualification; Have research knowledge related to, and skills in conducting quantitative studies; Proficiency in computer knowledge such as MS Office, SPSS Have a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese; Have a good interpersonal and communication skills; and Be able to work independently. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/53/HL/RA) Duties The Research Assistants (1) will play a key role in supporting a research project \"Comparative Critical Discourse Analysis of Song Lyrics (1964 to 1969) alongside the British Invasion to the U.S. & Second-Wave Feminism Discourse-Historical Approach \" focusing on data analysis of the qualitative data from lyrics by following the introduced analytical framework; (2) will work closely with the Principal Investigator; (3) will be responsible for various tasks, including data analysis and drafting research manuscripts for presentation/publication in conferences/journals; (4) may be required to assist in other related tasks as needed; (5) display the ability to work independently and to demonstrate willingness to learn. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized bachelor's degree or Sub-degree in any disciplines (preferably in Digital entertainment, IT or related disciplines concerning statistics); (b) research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English; and (f) proficiency in computer applications. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/44/HL/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project on: (a) administrative and coordinating work (b) collecting data and pre-processing them for experiments; (c) recruiting participants in experiments; (d) annotating data; (e) managing and updating datasets; (f) preparing reports; and (g) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized Bachelor's degree in humanities field; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English; and (f) proficiency in computer applications. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time / Part-time Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/33/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will be responsible to assist with the administrative duties and conduction of the research project. Tasks include: (a) literature review; (b) making arrangement to ensure a smooth research study; (c) collecting data and conducting data analysis; (d) preparing publications and reports; and (e) performing other assigned duties. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a bachelor's degree or above in health sciences or healthcare-related disciplines; (ii) 3-4 years of research experience and knowledge of mixed-methods research and survey design; (iii) knowledge in public health, community health and primary healthcare; (iv) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; and (v) good interpersonal, organizational and communication skills.  Those with 3 years' relevant experience or more may be considered for appointment as Senior Research Assistant. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/27/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator and the research team to support the research project. Duties include literature review, data collection and analysis, project management, report and manuscript writing and other related responsibilities as required. The appointee should be able to work independently and communicate in English and Chinese. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess at least a bachelor's degree in social science or relevant disciplines, with proficiency in SPSS/R/Python and other computer software, have knowledge and research skills in both quantitative and qualitative research, and/or have relevant research experience. Appointment will be made on contract basis, which can be renewed thereafter subject to funds available. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Associate, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/20/HL/RA) Duties The appointees will be responsible for various tasks relating to the Chinese culture project, which include (a) coordinating research design; (b) overseeing data collection and analysis; (c) writing academic publications and reports; (d) editing book series and academic journals; (e) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a doctoral degree in the humanities or relevant fields; (b) 3-4 years of research experience and knowledge of qualitative research; (c) strong background in research; (d) ability to work independently; (e) proficiency in writing in English and Chinese; (f) proficiency in communication and presentation skills. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/19/HL/RA) Duties The appointees will (a) assist the work of painting, drawing, animation, video production, and photography relating to the Chinese culture project; (b) assist the work of data collection and analysis; and (c) perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a bachelor's degree or master's degree in the humanities or relevant fields; (b) knowledge and skills of computer graphics; and (c) have good communication skills and sense of responsibility. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, S School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/05/CIS/RA) We are seeking a highly motivated and talented individual to join our team as a Research Assistant for the project \"AI in telehealth\". Duties The appointee will be responsible (a) collect and analyze data to evaluate the performance of the wet electrostatic precipitators and propose improvements; (b) contribute to the publication of research findings in scientific journals and present results at conferences; (c) work closely with the project lead and team members to ensure the project's objectives are met; and (d) assist in the supervision and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students involved in the project. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or related disciplines; (ii) have experience in statistical data; (iii) be able to work independently; (iv) have good communication and interpersonal skills; and (v) have good English writing skills. Applicants with publication experience are preferred. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled 2 Chui Ling Lane, Tseung Kwan O (Exit B, Tiu Keng Leng MTR Station), New Territories (852) 3702 4388 (852) 3653 6798 info@sfu.edu.hk Sitemap About SFU President's Message Overview of the University Governance Management Publications Academic Schools Non-Academic Units Admissions Why SFU Programmes by School Programmes by QF Level Admissions Admissions Portal Admission Hotlines Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance Admissions FAQ Programme Registration Student Support & Services Useful Information Services Scholarships, Bursaries and Financial Assistance College Life Useful Links Research Funded Projects Research Experts Research Highlights Research Office Research Centres and Laboratories Giving Home About Us Welcome Message Shatin Campus Development News & Event Research Matching Grant Scheme SFU Campus Acknowledgement Opportunities Give Now Our Donors Contact Us Global and Mainland Affairs About GMED Mainland Affairs